What was taken: `Zeta23/LinAlg/` only — the seven §3 linear-algebra files plus their root
module. Nothing from `Zeta23/FromPNTPlus/`, nothing from the analytic-number-theory half,
and none of the paper's headline theorems.

Apache-2.0 §4(d) says a NOTICE need not carry attributions that do not pertain to the
derivative work. Upstream's NOTICE credits PrimeNumberTheoremAnd (Alex Kontorovich et al.)
and mathlib for files under `Zeta23/FromPNTPlus/`. **No file from that directory is
present here**, so that attribution does not pertain to this port and is not reproduced as
an attribution — but upstream's NOTICE is retained verbatim beside this file as
`NOTICE.upstream` so a reader can check that judgement rather than take it on trust.

Modifications (Apache-2.0 §4(b)): every `.lean` file in this directory carries a
`MODIFIED FROM UPSTREAM` block naming its upstream path, the date, the work-item, the
Lean/Mathlib revisions it was retargeted between, and what changed. As of the initial
port the answer is "the notice block only" — the Lean content is byte-identical and no
proof needed re-proving at our pin.

Our own work sits OUTSIDE this directory and does not claim their copyright:
`src/Core.Lean4/Lean4/VonNeumannTraceWitness.lean`.
